    "title": "Stefon Diggs Compares Drake Maye's Maturation to Josh Allen's",
    "text": "• Stefon Diggs played with Josh Allen in Buffalo and now plays with Drake Maye in New England.\n• Diggs observed Allen's development from a promising quarterback to an elite MVP candidate.\n• In Allen's third NFL season (2020), he thrived with Diggs, throwing for 37 touchdowns and finishing second in MVP voting.\n• Diggs believes Maye's development has been exceptional.\n• Diggs stated that Allen is a 'hell of a player' and that he likes Maye's performance.\n• Allen ranks second in completion percentage (70.1%), fifth in passing touchdowns (22), and eighth in passing yards (3,085).\n• Allen has 487 rushing yards and 12 rushing touchdowns.\n• Maye ranks first in completion percentage (71.5%), second in passing yards (3,412), and has 23 passing touchdowns with six interceptions.\n• Maye and Allen are scheduled to play against each other on Sunday.\n• Allen praised Maye, noting his veteran-like play and great pace.\n• Conor Ryan is a staff writer for Boston.com covering the Bruins, Celtics, Patriots, and Red Sox since 2023.",
